---
// Standalone page — deliberately does NOT use ../layouts/BlogPost.astro.
// Privacy policy for "gordon-backup", the private Google OAuth app the Trustee's
// home server uses to back itself up to his own Google Drive. Hosted here only
// because Google requires a homepage + privacy policy URL to publish an OAuth app
// to production (Testing-mode tokens expire every 7 days). Not linked from anywhere,
// excluded from the sitemap (see astro.config.mjs). Christian, 2026-10-22.
// Same layout/styles as privacy-cardproai.astro.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="UTF-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
	<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
	<title>gordon-backup Privacy Policy</title>
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
	<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
	<style>
		:root {
			--bg: #0d1117;
			--surface: #161b22;
			--border: #30363d;
			--text: #c9d1d9;
			--muted: #8b949e;
			--accent: #58a6ff;
			--accent-dim: #1f3a5f;
		}
		* { box-sizing: border-box; }
		body {
			margin: 0;
			background: var(--bg);
			color: var(--text);
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif;
			line-height: 1.65;
		}
		.wrap {
			max-width: 680px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			padding: 64px 24px 80px;
		}
		.eyebrow {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.78rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.08em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			color: var(--accent);
			margin: 0 0 10px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: 2rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			margin: 0 0 6px;
			text-wrap: balance;
		}
		.meta {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			color: var(--muted);
			margin: 0 0 40px;
			display: flex;
			gap: 18px;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
		}
		.meta span { white-space: nowrap; }
		section {
			border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
			padding: 28px 0;
		}
		section:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
		h2 {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
			font-weight: 600;
			margin: 0 0 14px;
			display: flex;
			align-items: baseline;
			gap: 10px;
		}
		h2 .num {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			color: var(--accent);
			font-weight: 500;
		}
		p { margin: 0 0 12px; max-width: 62ch; }
		p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
		ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; max-width: 62ch; }
		li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
		strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
		.contact {
			margin-top: 40px;
			background: var(--surface);
			border: 1px solid var(--border);
			border-radius: 8px;
			padding: 18px 20px;
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.88rem;
		}
		.contact .label { color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 4px; }
		.contact a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
		.contact a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
		<h1>gordon-backup</h1>
		<p class="meta">
			<span>Effective 2026-10-22</span>
			<span>Private single-user tool</span>
		</p>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">1</span>What this is</h2>
			<p>
				gordon-backup is a private backup tool. It copies one individual's
				own home server to that same individual's own Google Drive account,
				so the server can be rebuilt if its hardware fails. It is not a
				public service, has no users other than its owner, and does not
				process data on behalf of anyone else.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">2</span>Information we access</h2>
			<p>
				Only the owner's own Google Drive, under an authorization the owner
				grants themselves. The tool uploads, updates, and removes the backup
				copies it maintains there.
			</p>
			<p>No data belonging to any other Google user is ever accessed.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">3</span>What we do not collect</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No account registration, no cookies, no visitor tracking or analytics on this page</li>
				<li>No personal data from anyone other than the owner</li>
				<li>No data is sold, rented, or shared with advertisers or any third party</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">4</span>How information is used</h2>
			<p>
				Solely to keep an off-site copy of the owner's own server for
				disaster recovery. Backup data is not analyzed, indexed, or used
				for any other purpose.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">5</span>Data storage &amp; security</h2>
			<p>
				The Google authorization is stored only on the owner's own server
				and is never transmitted anywhere except to Google's own APIs.
				The owner can revoke the authorization at any time from their Google account.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">6</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy may be updated if the tool's use of Google's APIs
				changes. The effective date above reflects the most recent revision.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</body>
</html>
